<%- include('../partials/header', { title, user: locals.user, layoutVariant: 'public' }) %>

<%
  const brandInfo = locals.brand || {};
  const supportName = brandInfo.supportContactName || brandInfo.orgName || 'our team';
  const supportEmail = brandInfo.supportContactEmail || '';
%>

<section class="page-header page-shell">
  <div>
    <a href="/events" class="btn-link">&larr; Back to sign-ups</a>
    <h1>Volunteer help</h1>
    <p class="muted">Plain-language steps for browsing events, signing up, fixing mistakes, and getting support. No tech skills required.</p>
    <% if (supportEmail) { %>
      <p class="muted small">Need direct help? Email <%= supportName %> at <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
    <% } else { %>
      <p class="muted small">Need direct help? Reply to your confirmation email and we’ll assist.</p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-section page-shell">
  <article class="card card--plain">
    <h2>Quick start</h2>
    <ol class="muted">
      <li>Open the <a href="/events">Sign-ups</a> page. Each event shows how many spots or items are still needed.</li>
      <li>Press “See what’s needed” on the event you want.</li>
      <li>Pick what you’d like to do, then tell us who’s coming. That’s it — no account or password.</li>
    </ol>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="page-section page-shell">
  <article class="card card--plain">
    <h2>If the event uses time slots</h2>
    <ol class="muted">
      <li>Step 1: Browse the stations and times. Each one shows how many spots are open. Use “Signing up:” at the top to choose who you’re signing up — yourself, or “Someone else…” (for example your kids) — then press “Sign up” on every spot for them. Use “View by time” or “Show only open spots” to narrow the list.</li>
      <li>Step 2: Type your name and email (you don’t have to fill a spot yourself). Check who is filling each spot and change it if needed.</li>
      <li>Press “Confirm sign-up.” You’ll see a summary on screen and get an email with a link to change things later.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted small">One person can’t take the same spot twice, or two spots at the same time. If someone is busy at that time, their name is greyed out and the spot says who is busy. When everyone in your group is busy, the button changes to “+ Someone else” so you can add another person. On a phone, a bar at the bottom shows how many spots you’ve picked — press “Continue” to jump to Step 2.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="page-section page-shell">
  <article class="card card--plain">
    <h2>If the event is Food Prep / Potluck</h2>
    <ol class="muted">
      <li>Step 1: Look through the items. Each shows how many are still needed and what others are already bringing. Press “Sign up” on the items you’ll bring.</li>
      <li>Step 2: Type your contact info. For each item, choose who is bringing it and type the dish name.</li>
      <li>Press “Confirm sign-up.” You’ll get an email with a link to change things later.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted small">Hints like “Feeds 6–8” show how big the dish should be. If an item is full, pick another.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="page-section page-shell">
  <article class="card card--plain">
    <h2>Seeing, adding to, or changing your sign-up</h2>
    <ol class="muted">
      <li>On the same phone or computer you signed up with, the event page shows “You’re signed up” with everything your group has, right at the top. Press “Add more or make changes.”</li>
      <li>On another device, use the link from your confirmation email. Lost it? On the event page, open “Already signed up? See what you have” and we’ll email it again.</li>
      <li>Your sign-up page lists what you already have first. Change who is filling a spot, remove spots, or add more from the list below, then press “Save changes.”</li>
      <li>To cancel everything, remove all your spots and save.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted small">Using a shared or public computer? Press “Not you? Start a new sign-up” on the event page so the next person doesn’t see your sign-up. Only the newest emailed link works, so if you ask for a new one, use that.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="page-section page-shell">
  <article class="card card--plain">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>“Already signed up … at this time”:</strong> that person already has another spot at the same time. Choose someone else, or remove one of the spots.</li>
      <li><strong>Spots show “Full”:</strong> choose another time or station; check back later in case more spots are added.</li>
      <li><strong>No confirmation email:</strong> check Promotions/Spam; request the link again from the event page; <% if (supportEmail) { %>or email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a><% } else { %>or try again later<% } %>.</li>
      <li><strong>“This email already has a sign-up”:</strong> each email has one sign-up per event. We email you the link right away — open it in the same browser and the spots you just picked will be waiting for you to save.</li>
      <li><strong>Can’t confirm:</strong> make sure you picked at least one spot, chose who fills each one, and typed your name and a valid email.</li>
      <li><strong>Went back to the events list?</strong> Your picks are kept in that browser tab until you confirm, so you can come back and finish.</li>
      <li><strong>On mobile:</strong> keep the page open until you see the thank-you screen.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="page-section page-shell">
  <article class="card card--plain">
    <h2>Need help?</h2>
    <% if (supportEmail) { %>
      <p class="muted">If you get stuck, email <%= supportName %> at <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>. Include the event name, the time/item you want, and your contact info.</p>
    <% } else { %>
      <p class="muted">If you get stuck, reply to your confirmation email with the event name, the time/item you want, and your contact info.</p>
    <% } %>
  </article>
</section>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
